.TH "RTCRTPTRANSCEIVER.MID" "3JS" "August 31, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCRtpTransceiver.mid \- RTCRtpTransceiver: mid property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The read\-only \f[CR]RTCRtpTransceiver\f[R] interface\(cqs
\f[B]\f[CB]mid\f[B]\f[R] property specifies the media ID
(\f[CR]mid\f[R]) which uniquely identifies the stream\(cqs pairing of
sender and receiver.
.SH VALUE
A string which uniquely identifies the pairing of source and destination
of the transceiver\(cqs stream.
Its value is taken from the media ID of the SDP m\-line.
This value is \f[CR]null\f[R] before a local or remote description
containing the corresponding m\-line is applied, or if a rollback undoes
that association.
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Introduction to the Real\-time Transport Protocol (RTP)
